Description: Implements the Soil Health Management Index (SHMI), a 0-100
    score of how strongly a field's management record supports soil health.
    It reads a standard Excel workbook of crop, tillage, amendment and animal
    records, and combines four sub-indices: living cover in the growing and
    non-growing seasons set by each site's climate, organic inputs, plant
    species richness and inverse tillage disturbance, with weights calibrated
    against measured soil health on US research sites. Every assumption made
    while reading the records is reported.
